<title>JAPAN: IBJ to cut June prime rate to 2.9%-banker.</title>
<headline>IBJ to cut June prime rate to 2.9%-banker.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd (IBJ) is expected to cut its prime lending rate to 2.9 percent in June, down from 3.1 percent in May, a long-term credit bank official said on Monday.</p>
<p>IBJ is scheduled to announce its June prime lending rate and the coupon rate for its new five-year bank debentures at 3.30 p.m. (0630 GMT) on Monday, IBJ officials said.</p>
